shadowsun-by-tonic (1.0+1-0ddebs8) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changes prepared with Claude Opus 5.5
  * debian/control : replaced the libsdl1.2-compat dependency, which does
    not exist on resolute and forky, by libsdl1.2-compat-shim, available
    (real or provided) on every distribution; build-depend on
    libglu1-mesa-dev first instead of the virtual libglu-dev; extended
    the description
  * debian/rules : removed the launcher generation and the dh_shlibdeps
    override, the shlibs now give the libsdl1.2debian dependency
  * debian/scripts : removed the launcher, which relied on
    common-install-function-ddebs without depending on it; the
    executable is run directly as /usr/bin/shadowsun-by-tonic
  * debian/resources : added the real icon (was an empty file), made
    from the screenshot of the compo results page
  * debian/resources/shadowsun-by-tonic.desktop : run the executable
    directly, added Keywords, Terminal and French entries
  * debian/patches/01_adapt_makefile.patch : use CPPFLAGS for hardening
    (_FORTIFY_SOURCE), rebuild when the source changes, DEP-3 header
  * debian/patches/02_enable_vsync.patch : enable vertical
    synchronization (SDL_GL_SWAP_CONTROL)
  * debian/shadowsun-by-tonic.6.md : fixed description, documented the
    Escape key, regenerated the manual page
  * debian/shadowsun-by-tonic.lintian-overrides : removed the Keywords
    override, added the pandoc groff-message override
  * debian/README.source : documented the patches

 -- Nicolas HOUDELOT <nicolas@demosdebs.org>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:25:34 +0100

